# The member that killed additive pricing. Five positive-marginal attributes stacked in one recipe --
# labelwise head, distill at w=0.7, blend-three labels, calib-tgt, hold-annot -- on top of a teacher
# (teacher_foreign_corpus.npz) that is ~80% exposed to fold 0 by construction. Under strict additivity
# its 0%-pool marginals promise 0.9032; the saturation curve fitted before it finished predicted
# 0.865-0.867; it landed 0.8634, CONVERGED, peaking at epoch 8 of 12. So it does not reach the honest
# pool max 0.8649 despite carrying more positive attributes than any member that does, and it is the
# second member ever to sit in the k=5 bin (chainfour_s2026, 0.8648, was the first and only). Rostered
# because it is the strongest evidence on disk that attribute terms rank rather than add, and because a
# k=5 member is worth a seat TEST even below the max -- never because its solo number earns one.
# EXPOSURE: ~80%, non-zero. It fails the fourth honesty filter and must not enter an entry whose
# offline number is quoted as clean. Its 0%-exposure twin distill_stack_clean_s2026 is the control.
distill_stack_max_s2026.pt           # 0.8634 -- ~80% teacher exposure, NOT clean

# THE BEST HONEST SOLO THIS PROJECT OWNS, and the first member on either shelf trained with stochastic
# depth. 0.8654 @holdout909 midpoint, epoch 12 of 12, fold 0, every holdout study out-of-sample, 0%
# teacher exposure. It passes all four honesty filters and may be quoted in a clean offline number.
# It edges clean_calib_s2026 (0.8649) by +0.0005, which is noise -- the seat case is NOT the solo number.
# The seat case is DIVERSITY OF MECHANISM: every other member on both shelves was trained with the trunk
# fully connected on every step, and this one samples a different sub-network per sample per step. That
# is a source of decorrelation no recipe knob on this roster produces, and the owner's standing rule is
# that a member earns a seat test on diversity even when it does not outperform.
# CAVEAT: it PEAKED ON ITS LAST EPOCH and was still climbing, so 0.8654 is a FLOOR for this recipe, not
# its converged value. dropstack_long_s2026 (24 epochs, same rate, knee-ffku5) is the arm that reads the
# converged number; if it lands, prefer it for the seat and keep this one as the 12-epoch control.
dropstack_light_s2026.pt             # 0.8654 -- best honest solo, stochastic depth 0.05, budget-bound
dropstack_long_s2026.pt              # 0.8641 @e13 -- the 24-epoch twin of dropstack_light. Its OWN bottom
                            # band (-0.0013): budget is closed as a lever at the max-pooling corner, and
                            # there is no late peak to blame the stretched one-cycle for (peak e13, then
                            # eleven declining epochs). Seated on DIVERSITY, not quality. It disagrees
                            # with dropstack_light on six labels in each direction, up to 0.018 on a
                            # single one, at a mean distance of 0.0013 -- two runs of one recipe that
                            # order studies differently. The 2026-09-12 board read is that decorrelation,
                            # not member quality, is the only channel that has ever added board points.

# THE 0.40 SLOT-DROPOUT DOSE, and the first member on either shelf rostered on a CROSS-SITE number
# rather than on holdout909. Added 2026-09-12. Its own-holdout 0.8551 is 0.0027 BELOW its matched
# control band_dense_s2026 (0.8578), and that is not a trade-off to be weighed -- holdout909 is drawn
# from the same decode as training, so it is blind BY CONSTRUCTION to the axis this member exists for.
# The two numbers measure different things and only the second is about how the real test set differs
# from us. Do not rank it against the pool on 0.8551.
#
# WHAT IT IS ROSTERED ON. Its foreign decode toll is -0.0229 against the control's -0.0361: +0.0132
# shallower, 3.5 sd of the eleven-member pool the toll was calibrated on. The 0.25 dose already on the
# first shelf reads +0.0090 / 2.4 sd. Three doses, one direction -- 0.00 -0.0361, 0.25 -0.0271,
# 0.40 -0.0229 -- and monotone through the last measured point, which is what makes slot dropout a
# recipe TERM rather than one lucky checkpoint. Calibration gate passed: the control reproduced -0.0361
# exactly and slot_cost landed inside +/-0.0001 on both rows. Bead knee-lhico, ledger 2026-09-12.
#
# THE SEAT QUESTION IT ASKS is a straight dose A/B against slot_dropout_s2026 in one seat, and 0 of the
# board's rows name it. It does NOT claim the 0.40 dose is optimal: monotone through the last point
# leaves 0.55 open, and one foreign corpus is one point on transfer.
slot_dropout_hi_s2026.pt             # 0.8551 -- the 0.40 dose; seated on decode, see above

# THE SECOND SITE, WHICH HAS NEVER REACHED THE BOARD. Both members below are fitted on the KMAR-50K
