                            # labelwise_depth24's line with --slot-dropout 0.40 and --epochs 24, nothing
                            # else (knee-9bnkc). CLEARS ITS BAND: +0.0055 ledger75 over
                            # labelwise_depth24_s2026 0.8998, its pre-registered >= +0.0040.
                            # convergence_check returns CONVERGED and the peak is e18, NOT the last
                            # epoch, so the header's veto clause never fires; per knee-a21h9 the verdict
                            # is read from the check either way, never by argmax.
                            # SECOND MATCHED BASE. With knee-cgt9m (+0.0059 on labelwise_extended) the
                            # slot-dropout-0.40 + doubled-budget operator pair is established off the
                            # `max` pooling corner on n=2 bases, not n=1. That is what licenses applying
                            # the pair to the rest of the labelwise family without re-proving it.
                            # Rostered on QUALITY. No seating for it has been priced against the
                            # champion yet -- its twin at 0.9045 added +0.0017 as a seventh seat, under
                            # the +0.0040 floor, and this member correlates with the same consensus.
labelwise_dense_drop40_long_s2026.pt    # 0.8672 mid (l75 0.9048, e23 of 0..23) -- THIRD AND LAST
                            # MATCHED BASE for the slot-dropout-0.40 + doubled-budget operator pair
                            # (knee-vs06j). labelwise_dense's line with --slot-dropout 0.40 and
                            # --epochs 24, nothing else. CLEARS ITS BAND BY THE WIDEST MARGIN OF THE
                            # THREE: +0.0084 ledger75 over labelwise_dense_s2026 0.8964, against a
                            # pre-registered >= +0.0040. Its base peaked EARLIEST of the family (e7 of
                            # 12), which is the strongest form of the missing-regulariser signature,
                            # and it gained the most -- the two agree.
                            # ITS ARGMAX IS ITS LAST EPOCH, and the header's hand-written veto would
                            # refuse the verdict. The legislated rule (knee-a21h9) is convergence_check,
                            # which asks for argmax-last AND a final-three-epoch gain clearing the
                            # 0.0062 holdout floor. e21 0.8670, e22 0.8670, e23 0.8672: a tail gain of
                            # +0.0002, a thirtieth of the floor, and the check returns CONVERGED.
                            # SEATED ON QUALITY AND ON ADDITIVITY. Measured 2026-09-13, full 909,
                            # LogitAverage, no selection, against the honest core six at 0.9050:
                            #   + depth_up + ext_up (the eight)      0.9081  +0.0031
                            #   + all three (the nine)               0.9090  +0.0040
                            #   swapped core + depth_up + ext_up     0.9089  +0.0039
                            # The nine CLEARS the +0.0040 seat floor, and the swap of this member for
                            # its own base buys the same +0.0039 at eight seats rather than nine.
                            # Additivity is decelerating (+0.0020, +0.0011, +0.0009 per added base),
                            # which is what knee-fnhbs's fourth base is pre-registered to read.
labelwise_ext_drop40_long_ff.pt         # DARK BY CONSTRUCTION -- fitted with `--fold -1`, so it holds out
                            # nothing and no ledger row can ever price it. Rostered anyway, and the
                            # argument is its TWIN: `labelwise_ext_drop40_long_s2026` is the same recipe
                            # line on fold 0 and reads 0.9045 ledger75, the second-best honest solo the
                            # project owns, seated in kneemri-tripleseat. A full-fit refit of a member
                            # that clears the seat floor is the same shape as every one of the champion's
                            # six (`final_ws_cf`, `calib_span_ff`, ...), which are all `--fold -1` and all
                            # unscoreable here -- so this is the project's ordinary way of turning a
                            # measured recipe into a shippable seat, not an exception to it.
                            # WHAT IT IS NOT: evidence. It may be seated, and it may never be quoted as a
                            # number. Any entry carrying it reads on the BOARD or not at all.
labelwise_depth24_drop40_long_ff.pt     # DARK BY CONSTRUCTION -- `--fold -1 --ema`, holds out nothing, so
                            # no ledger row can price it. Rostered on its TWIN, exactly as
                            # `labelwise_ext_drop40_long_ff` above: `labelwise_depth24_drop40_long_s2026`
                            # is the same recipe on fold 0 at 0.9053 ledger75, the best honest solo owned,
                            # seated in kneemri-tripleseat. Finished 24 of 24 epochs 2026-09-15. It may be
                            # seated and never quoted; any entry carrying it reads on the BOARD.
depth24_ff_long36.pt        # DARK BY CONSTRUCTION -- `--fold -1 --ema`. The depth24_ff line above with
                            # `--epochs 36` and nothing else moved (knee-lz8pd), 36 of 36 epochs, ARM DONE.
                            # Its board control is `labelwise_depth24_drop40_long_ff` at 0.944, so a solo
                            # entry reads the schedule term alone. Seated only in its own solo kernel.
dml_b_ff.pt                 # DARK BY CONSTRUCTION -- `--fold -1`, the third refit of this family and the
                            # one that makes the other two READABLE. Its twin `dml_b_s2026` is 0.9078
                            # ledger75, the highest this project owns, +0.0025 over the depth24 twin above.
                            # THAT EDGE IS NOT WHY IT IS HERE, and the roster's own `dml_b` line says why:
                            # the offline ruler does not order at the top, so 0.9078 predicts board 0.942
                            # as an UPPER bound. It is rostered as the third point of an ADDITIVE-vs-CEILING
                            # test, because the two refits above already read CEILING -- fold-0 twins 0.937
                            # and 0.941 (spread 0.004) refit to 0.945 and 0.944 (spread 0.001, ORDER
                            # INVERTED). A refit that erases a recipe gap is a ceiling, not an addition.
                            # ADDITIVE lands it ~0.947-0.950, CEILING ~0.9445, and CEILING is the favourite
                            # at P(clears 0.945) ~ 0.20. See knee-8bmi2 for the pre-registration.
                            # It may be seated and never quoted; any entry carrying it reads on the BOARD.
dml_b_ff_long36.pt          # DARK BY CONSTRUCTION -- `--fold -1 --ema`. dml_b_ff above with `--epochs 36`
                            # and nothing else moved (knee-bxp8h), 36 of 36 epochs, ARM DONE 19:59Z. It
                            # carries the peer term and the long anneal together; its controls are the two
                            # solo entries of dml_b_ff and depth24_ff_long36. Seated only in its own solo kernel.

# ---- the operator pair, five members found already on disk and priced 2026-09-13 ----
# `roster_check` named seven undocumented checkpoints and five of them were `drop40_long` runs nobody had
# priced. So the pair (`--slot-dropout 0.40` + `--epochs 12 -> 24`) had already been run far wider than the
# five bases the labelwise work knew about. ledger75, 909 rows, `--holdouts D:/models/rsna_knee_abnormality`:
#
#   band_dense_drop40_long 0.8918 @e16  vs band_dense 0.8877 @e8   +0.0041
#   base224_drop40_long    0.8865 @e17  vs base224    0.8795 @e9   +0.0070
#   base224_drop40_long_run1 0.8855 @e17 same base                 +0.0060   (DECLINED, seed)
#   severity_drop40_long   0.8899 @e18  base HAS NO LEDGER ROW     UNREAD
#   mergedk_drop40_long    0.8853 @e17  base HAS NO LEDGER ROW     UNREAD
#
# That takes the pair to SEVEN of seven measurable bases clearing +0.0040 -- depth24 +0.0055, ext +0.0059,
# dense +0.0084, chainfour +0.0070, blendhold +0.0050, band_dense +0.0041, base224 +0.0070 -- across four
# unrelated recipe families. And base224's two seeds are a FREE REPLICATION of the operator itself: +0.0070
# and +0.0060, a seed spread of 0.0010 against an effect of ~0.0065. That is the first seed-level error bar
# this project has on the pair, and it is an order of magnitude below the effect.
#
# WHAT THESE FOUR ARE AND ARE NOT. Each is a solo number, not a seat. None of their bases is in the honest
# core six, so none is a SWAP candidate for that pool -- they are ADD candidates, and the ADD reading is the
# weak one (measured 2026-09-13: chainfour_up adds +0.0007 as a seventh seat while swapping for +0.0012).
# None may be seated until it is priced as a marginal over the pool it would join. Rostered so it CAN be.
band_dense_drop40_long_s2026.pt         # 0.8918 ledger75 @e16 of 0..23, 909 rows. The operator pair on
                            # `band_dense`, +0.0041 over its base at 0.8877 @e8 -- the base peaks at 8 of
                            # 12 and declines, the missing-regulariser signature, and the pair closes it.
                            # The smallest of the seven gains and still at the seat floor.
severity_drop40_long_s2026.pt           # 0.8899 ledger75 @e18 of 0..23, 909 rows. UNREAD AS A DELTA:
                            # `severity_s2026` returned NO ROW from ledger75 (requested, silently omitted
                            # -- the tool prints nothing for a stem it has no holdout record for, so count
                            # returned rows against requested stems). The +N here is not known and must not
                            # be quoted. Its SOLO stands on its own and is mid-pool.
base224_drop40_long_s2026.pt            # 0.8865 ledger75 @e17 of 0..23, 909 rows. +0.0070 over `base224`
                            # at 0.8795 @e9 -- tied with chainfour as the largest gain the pair has
                            # produced, on the project's plainest recipe. A second run of this exact
                            # recipe exists and is DECLINED in comp/members.declines (seeds are banned);
                            # it read 0.8855, and the pair of them is the operator's only replication.
mergedk_drop40_long_s2026.pt            # 0.8853 ledger75 @e17 of 0..23, 909 rows. UNREAD AS A DELTA:
                            # `mergedk_s2026` returned NO ROW from ledger75, same omission as severity.
                            # READ THE DECLINE ABOVE BEFORE SEATING THIS: the KMAR second-site merge was
                            # declined 2026-09-13 as a measured null (+0.0005 marginal against a +0.0040
                            # pre-registration), and this is the same corpus with the pair on top. The
                            # operator lifting a member does not re-open an axis that was closed on its
                            # MARGINAL value -- that decline is answered by a marginal, not by a solo.
blendhold_drop40_long_s2026.pt          # 0.8879 ledger75 @e19 of 0..23, 909 rows. The operator pair on
                            # `blendhold`, +0.0050 over its base at 0.8829. SEATED AS A SWAP, NOT AS AN
                            # ADD, and the distinction is measured rather than argued. Against the honest
                            # core six at 0.9050, full 909, LogitAverage, no selection (2026-09-13):
                            #   added as a seventh seat                +0.0000
                            #   swapped for `blendhold_s2026`          +0.0008
                            # It clears the operator band SOLO and then adds nothing on top of the base it
                            # duplicates -- the correlated-duplicate signature. Remove the base and the
                            # same member pays. Any entry carrying it must DROP `blendhold_s2026`; seating
                            # both is the +0.0000 reading, and that is the whole finding.

# ---- the fourth base, and the ADD/SWAP correction it forced (2026-09-13) ----
# `labelwise_drop_drop40_long` is the EIGHTH base to clear the operator pair's +0.0040 floor and the ONLY
# member of eleven that does not COST when added to the best seating. Priced as a SWAP it is worth more
# than any add the project has measured. Read the two readings as the two different questions they are.
labelwise_drop_drop40_long_s2026.pt      # 0.9051 ledger75 @e18 of 0..23, 909 rows, convergence_check
                            # converged. +0.0067 over `labelwise_drop_s2026` at 0.8984 @e10 -- eighth of
                            # eight bases for the pair (`--slot-dropout 0.40` + `--epochs 12 -> 24`).
                            # It is the POOL'S JOINT TOP solo, tied with `labelwise_depth24_drop40_long`
                            # at 0.9053, and the only member ever measured above `foreign_oof_corpus`.
                            #
                            # AS AN ADD it is worth +0.0004 on the n=7 four-swap core + depth_up (0.9093)
                            # -- directional, knee-fnhbs closed on that band, no slot was spent on it.
                            # AS A SWAP it is worth +0.0011, replacing `clean_calib_s2026` (solo 0.8940)
                            # with n held at 7: 0.9093 -> 0.9103, the best seating this project has
                            # measured. An entry carrying it that way must DROP `clean_calib_s2026`.
                            # SEATING BOTH IS THE +0.0004 READING, not the +0.0011 one.
                            #
                            # THE CAVEAT THAT KEEPS IT OFF A SLOT ON ITS OWN: +0.0011 is the argmax of
                            # seven swaps chosen on the holdout, and a beam over all 28 priced members
                            # reaches only 0.9113 with FIVE seatings tied there to four decimals --
                            # holdout selection, the defect that left `cleanseat_v1` `offline: None,
                            # scope: excluded`. board_transfer +1.135 puts +0.0011 at ~+0.0012 against a
                            # board that reports at 0.001. Ship it inside a POOL move, never as a
                            # thirteenth reseating (knee-tuzzp, and goldseat_v1's note: twelve seating
                            # entries have now failed to beat 0.944).

stack_increments_drop40_long_s2026.pt   # 0.8951 ledger75 @e16 of 0..23, 909 rows, converged. The
                            # operator pair (`--slot-dropout 0.40` + `--epochs 12 -> 24`) on
                            # `stack_increments_s2026` 0.8931 @e9 = +0.0020, against a pre-registered
                            # +0.0040 floor (knee-p29bb). NINTH base tried and the FIRST to miss: the
                            # eight before it spanned four recipe families at +0.0041..+0.0084. What is
                            # different here is the corner -- distillation plus blended labels -- and
                            # that corner is the champion's own.
                            # DO NOT SEAT IT AS AN UPGRADE OF ITS BASE. Measured in the same sitting
                            # (`<scratchpad>/twin_twoout.py`): with this member standing in place of
                            # `stack_increments_s2026`, the best n=8 twin seating reads 0.9097 against
                            # 0.9098 with the plain base. -0.0001. It is rostered because it is the
                            # instrument that closed knee-289qc's twelve-hour blind refit, not because
                            # a seating wants it. Re-open by pricing it as a marginal, never by a solo.

# ---- the operator pair's TENTH base, and the first whose gain is only at the 0.75 cut (2026-09-13) ----
clean_calib_drop40_long_s2026.pt        # 0.8978 ledger75 @e23 of 0..23, 909 rows, convergence_check
                            # converged. The operator pair (`--slot-dropout 0.40` + `--epochs 12 -> 24`)
                            # on `clean_calib_s2026` 0.8940 @e9 = +0.0038, against the family's
                            # pre-registered +0.0040 floor. TENTH base tried, SECOND to miss it, and it
                            # misses by 0.0002 -- inside the noise of the floor itself, so read it as the
                            # band's edge rather than as a refutation of the pair here.
                            #
                            # WHAT IS ACTUALLY NEW: THE MIDPOINT IS FLAT TO NEGATIVE. 0.8649 -> 0.8647,
                            # -0.0002, while ledger75 moves +0.0038. Those are the SAME predictions under
                            # two binarisations of the same graded truth, so a gain that exists only at
                            # 0.75 is a gain in how the member ranks the CONFIDENT positives (truth >=
                            # 0.75) against everything else, with none in the ranking the 0.5 cut sees.
                            # Every other base for this pair moved both rulers together. This one says
                            # the pair can buy confident-case discrimination alone, which is the half of
                            # the graded truth the board is mostly made of -- and it is also why this
                            # member may not be quoted at midpoint in either direction.
                            #
                            # NOT YET SEATED. A solo is not a seat (`stack_increments` read +0.0020 solo
                            # and -0.0001 seated). Price it as a SWAP for `clean_calib_s2026`, which the
                            # champion six holds, and an entry carrying it that way must DROP that member.
# MOVED TO SHELF 1, 2026-09-16 -- named on BOTH rosters, and once shelf 1 was re-pushed with its
# full 147 members that duplicate became LIVE: MemberPackage.absorb refuses a name held by two
# mounts, so a kernel mounting both shelves would have died on WeightsError rather than dropping
# a seat. It is served from `dimiturnt/kneemri-members` now; the seat is unchanged, only its
# shelf. The roster-level duplicate predates the push -- roster_check's `packaged` is a SET, so
# it merged the two names silently instead of naming them, and only mount_check saw it (knee-aqppc).
# warm_calib_lowlr_drop40_long_s2026.pt   # 0.9000 ledger75 @e8, 909 rows, convergence_check TRUNCATED (the
                            # PC shut down mid-run) so the number is a FLOOR. On `warm_calib_lowlr_s2026`
                            # 0.8910 @e4 that is +0.0090 -- the operator pair's largest gain on any base,
                            # and a floor. NOT YET SEATED; price as a SWAP for its control, re-run to finish.
